  "environment": {
    "Overview": "Components of industrial style include weathered wood, building systems, exposed brick, industrial lighting fixtures, and concrete. Industrial style can also be seen in the use of unexpected materials used in building. Shipping containers are now being used in architecture for homes and commercial spaces. The industrial style of design is most commonly found in urban areas, including cities and lofts. These are prime locations because they provide almost a blank space for homeowners to get started with a fresh canvas."
  },
